course: dictionary
lesson: 6127
title: Words for people who help
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words name a job. Read the words around a new word to find its meaning. «A midwife is a nurse trained to care for women and babies during pregnancy, birth and the first days after.» The sentence tells you the job: a nurse who looks after mums and babies.
explain: Look at the clues in «Two Hebrew midwives, Shiphrah and Puah, refused Pharaoh's order to kill the baby boys.» Midwives are helpers at births, and they say no to a wrong order. Ask yourself: what would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
explain: Words can also be used in a bigger way. A midwife can be a person who helps something new to come into being. This is called figurative use, and you can spot it when the meaning goes beyond a real job.
fact: Midwife is a noun. Its plural is midwives.
fact: A midwife is a trained nurse or health worker who helps women while they are pregnant, while they give birth and just afterwards.
fact: In stories set long ago, the village midwife delivered babies at home.
fact: Phrases to know: community midwife, and the midwife delivered the baby.
fact: Figurative meaning: a person who helps something new to come into being.
exercise: «A midwife is a nurse trained to care for women and babies during pregnancy, birth and the first days after.» What is a midwife? | A person who sells bread at the market | *A trained nurse who helps women and babies | A teacher who runs a village school
exercise: «The midwife delivered the baby.» What does delivered mean here? | Wrapped the baby in a warm blanket | *Helped the baby be born | Sent the baby a letter in the post | Carried the baby somewhere far away
exercise: «Two Hebrew midwives, Shiphrah and Puah, refused Pharaoh's order to kill the baby boys.» Which word means said no to? | *refused | midwives | Pharaoh | baby
test: «Our new science teacher was a midwife to my love of stars.» What does midwife mean here? | *A person who helped a new interest come into being | A person who sells books about space | A nurse who works in a hospital | A person who makes telescopes
test: What is the plural of midwife? | *midwives | midwifes | midwife's | midwivs
exam: «In stories set long ago, the village midwife delivered babies at home.» What does a midwife do? | Builds houses for families in the village | Drives the bus to the market | Paints pictures of the hills | *Helps women during pregnancy and birth, and checks the new baby
